      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Key examples illustrating this concept include *Griswold v. Connecticut*, which established a constitutional right to marital privacy, and *Roe v. Wade*, which addressed reproductive privacy rights. More recently, *Lawrence v. Texas* protected laws against same-sex intimacy. These cases demonstrate the Supreme Court's use of substantive due process to recognize and protect fundamental rights that were not explicitly detailed in the Constitution's text.",
      "source": "target",
